<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 26.17 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 26.17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of 12-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 26.17 percent at auction on April 7 from 27.49 percent at the last auction on March 10, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   April 7	    March 10</p>
<p> Series number		  KZ4CK0904987	KZ4CK1203983</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  350		    300</p>
<p> Bids (nominal,bln tenge)	  1.4		    1.9</p>
<p> Sold (nominal)			350		    300</p>
<p> Average price			 79.26 pct	    78.44</p>
<p> Average yield			 26.17 pct	    27.49</p>
<p> Tenor				   364 days	     364 days</p>
<p> Maturity			     April 9, 1997     March 12, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
